```

**Branch B — Normal loading from Output Voucher** — lines 855-859:
```21:21:g:\0.CMS-MAIN-ALL\-vat-tuquangbin\StockManager\Voucher\Output\frmOutputVoucherDetail.cs
                SMS_OutputVoucherDetail objDetail = new SMS_OutputVoucherDetail();
                dtbData = objDetail.GetList(lngOutputVoucherID);
```

After both branches, two columns are **added programmatically** (lines 862-870):
```30:38:g:\0.CMS-MAIN-ALL\-vat-tuquangbin\StockManager\Voucher\Output\frmOutputVoucherDetail.cs
                // thêm cột chọn hàng để xuất
                if (!dtbData.Columns.Contains("IsSelected"))
                    dtbData.Columns.Add("IsSelected", typeof(Boolean));
                foreach (DataRow drw in dtbData.Rows)
                    drw["IsSelected"] = true;

                // thêm cột OutputVoucherDetailIDTemp để SaveDetail có thể gán sau khi ADD
                if (!dtbData.Columns.Contains("OutputVoucherDetailIDTemp"))
                    dtbData.Columns.Add("OutputVoucherDetailIDTemp", typeof(Int64));
```

### 3. From Output Order (line 1813 in `uOutputOrder_EditValueChanged`)
```csharp
dtbData = objDetail.GetDataTable("SMS_OutputOrderDetail_OutputVoucherDetail", "@OutputOrderID", uOutputOrder.OutputOrderID);
```

> **Important**: The actual column schema of `dtbData` comes from whichever stored procedure populates it (`SMS_OutputVoucherDetail_GetList`, `GetListReturnInput`, or `SMS_OutputOrderDetail_OutputVoucherDetail`). The code only references columns by name; it does **not** explicitly construct a `DataTable` schema in this file.

